time="2026-11-03T12:37:20.927-05:00" level=info msg="Final message: \"In-Reply-To: <MN2PR07MB59186154ED809FE0BC12F683C0692@MN2PR07MB5918.namprd07.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nMIME-Version: 1.0\\r\\nReferences: <MN2PR07MB59188388A51F44B3CD508E96C0602@MN2PR07MB5918.namprd07.prod.outlook.com> <CABAFTuv_ugieRfmjG6+rfRb377eFQDW5qNDfFzo1qrBzx8kYhQ@mail.gmail.com> <CABAFTuuLPh2snoVJB1rqU83kC5AjU=y00TGZHE348TaKJxAp_A@mail.gmail.com> <MN2PR07MB59188CE9E5189DDC994F36D4C0602@MN2PR07MB5918.namprd07.prod.outlook.com> <CABAFTutDnRO0Qc40PLPsY1PMHMv+GZUmz-PE2SQ7ZUM__vqNVA@mail.gmail.com> <MN2PR07MB5918C878B5DB77D5CD54F2F5C0602@MN2PR07MB5918.namprd07.prod.outlook.com> <CABAFTus0WwEpGwR3x8L4R66teQKZeGJ-3u6t_GgVLnpfHA8fvg@mail.gmail.com> <MN2PR07MB5918A9FFE0F70B6BC1B362B4C06F2@MN2PR07MB5918.namprd07.prod.outlook.com> <MN2PR07MB5918EE98E6FBB69F610FBF81C06A2@MN2PR07MB5918.namprd07.prod.outlook.com> <CABAFTutY3bHX1t+pJt3-L_CXeAsfp2H57bA=__dMWxW=ueBKVg@mail.gmail.com> <CABAFTuvv6d__0nCDGXmD7orwdTLn4AGV-_taAtFqmXP9p74Y-w@mail.gmail.com> <MN2PR07MB5918DF0D4332CA585C38AEBDC06A2@MN2PR07MB5918.namprd07.prod.outlook.com> <CABAFTusN6xoDN=oa78nm66JisT4V0C8gT1vZhUjiGbdwJT4L8w@mail.gmail.com> <MN2PR07MB59184B07AECCB5EE7F6F6B3DC0692@MN2PR07MB5918.namprd07.prod.outlook.com> <CABAFTuudQXu5vJwOyERFh-RNFWELvkTsh40uVDx_mHDmvHLVuA@mail.gmail.com> <MN2PR07MB59186154ED809FE0BC12F683C0692@MN2PR07MB5918.namprd07.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nSubject: Re: Ardia\\r\\nTo: \\\"Bott, Alex Joseph\\\" <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu>\\r\\nContent-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=\\\"5cce1de54cc5868dab01203aeb6a29fbb11f54543a3597a340f8e8526e78\\\"\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\n\\r\\n--5cce1de54cc5868dab01203aeb6a29fbb11f54543a3597a340f8e8526e78\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nOkay! It's all back up now.\\n\\nOn Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:17:18 -0500, \\\"Bott, Alex Joseph\\\" <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu> said:\\n> No worries. I probably won't start anything until tomorrow since I need to have Yuchen help me mount to standby.\\n> ________________________________\\n> From: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu>\\n> Sent: Tuesday, November 3, 2026 11:45 AM\\n> To: Bott, Alex Joseph <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu>\\n> Subject: Re: Ardia\\n>\\n> No problem! By the way, I do need to unplug the network switch briefly\\n> to rearrange some cables--I saw you're not currently logged in, but\\n> just FYI network access will be down for a minute while I do that.\\n>\\n> On Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:33:20 -0500, \\\"Bott, Alex Joseph\\\"\\n> <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu> said:\\n>> Awesome! Thanks again for managing the machine and dealing with this all!\\n>> ________________________________\\n>> From: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu>\\n>> Sent: Tuesday, November 3, 2026 11:31 AM\\n>> To: Bott, Alex Joseph <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu>\\n>> Subject: Re: Ardia\\n>>\\n>> It works now! New IP is 10.119.48.62\\n>>\\n>> On Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:23:50 -0500, \\\"Bott, Alex Joseph\\\"\\n>> <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu> said:\\n>>> Roger that, thanks again!\\n>>> ________________________________\\n>>> From: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu>\\n>>> Sent: Monday, November 2, 2026 4:34 PM\\n>>> To: Bott, Alex Joseph <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu>\\n>>> Subject: Re: Ardia\\n>>>\\n>>> Sounds like the issue is due to the switchbox that is between the\\n>>> computer and the wall socket. He said a guy will come by tomorrow\\n>>> morning to sort it out.\\n>>>\\n>>> On Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:59:10 -0500, \\\"Lindgren, Caleb\\\"\\n>>> <clindgren@g.harvard.edu> said:\\n>>>> Unfortunately nothing yet. I emailed Peter on Friday evening and told him it still wasn't working, and he said he'd have them look into it more on Monday, but that's the last I heard. I'll ping him again.\\n>>>>\\n>>>> On Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:55:59 -0500, \\\"Bott, Alex Joseph\\\" <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu> said:\\n>>>>> Hey Caleb,\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> Just wanted to see if there was any update. I'm eager to start looking at my last DIA data but understand if IT is slow rolling it.\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> Thanks,\\n>>>>> Alex\\n>>>>> ________________________________\\n>>>>> From: Bott, Alex Joseph <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu>\\n>>>>> Sent: Wednesday, October 28, 2026 2:39 PM\\n>>>>> To: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu>\\n>>>>> Subject: Re: Ardia\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> Ok sounds good, thanks for the update! I'll be in tomorrow and can help if needed.\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> Thanks for managing this! I think I'll back up my data on the Ardia to O2 tonight just in case.\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> Best,\\n>>>>> Alex\\n>>>>> ________________________________\\n>>>>> From: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu>\\n>>>>> Sent: Wednesday, October 28, 2026 2:35 PM\\n>>>>> To: Bott, Alex Joseph <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu>\\n>>>>> Subject: Re: Ardia\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> Just FYI, the guys getting us the new table that we're going to put the Ardia on in the new room said they actually can't bring the table until tomorrow, so we're going to have to wait until tomorrow to move it. I'll keep you posted.\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> Bott, Alex Joseph <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu<mailto:alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu>> 於 2026年10月27日週二 15:05 寫道：\\n>>>>> Ah man ok. Well I'll just log in and survey the damage. I think I had logging points along the run but let's see.\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> Thanks for taking care of everything. Very hopeful that the new home will further reduce issues.\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> Best,\\n>>>>> Alex\\n>>>>> ________________________________\\n>>>>> From: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu<mailto:clindgren@g.harvard.edu>>\\n>>>>> Sent: Tuesday, October 27, 2026 3:03 PM\\n>>>>> To: Bott, Alex Joseph <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu<mailto:alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu>>\\n>>>>> Subject: Re: Ardia\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> Yeah, it was spontaneous. JP said he hadn't touched it or noticed\\n>>>>> anything weird. The cover was displaced when I came in this morning,\\n>>>>> so maybe it just got bumped.\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> What I ended up doing was unplugging the power, taking off the cover,\\n>>>>> taking out the fan cage and airflow distributor, and then reseating\\n>>>>> some cables that the logs flagged as having issues. Unsure exactly\\n>>>>> which step fixed it, but the diagnostics all look good now. I checked\\n>>>>> on Docker and everything was gone, so I went ahead and did the Sysbox\\n>>>>> install.\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> Good to go now, but I wouldn't start anything today that will still be\\n>>>>> running tomorrow--JP said he's got someone coming in tomorrow to\\n>>>>> install a table in the supply room closet between Shelly and David's\\n>>>>> benches, so we'll power the machine off and move it there tomorrow.\\n>>>>> Hopefully putting it in a more isolated environment will fix these\\n>>>>> issues we've been having.\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> Thanks for your help with this!\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> On Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:23:13 -0400, \\\"Bott, Alex Joseph\\\"\\n>>>>> <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu<mailto:alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu>> said:\\n>>>>>> Sounds good, I assume it went down spontaneously? If the machine fully went down I bet my long running jobs died, so maybe that would indicate a good time for your docker fix.\\n>>>>>> ________________________________\\n>>>>>> From: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu<mailto:clindgren@g.harvard.edu>>\\n>>>>>> Sent: Tuesday, October 27, 2026 1:14 PM\\n>>>>>> To: Bott, Alex Joseph <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu<mailto:alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu>>\\n>>>>>> Subject: Re: Ardia\\n>>>>>>\\n>>>>>> It boots now, but I'm still debugging so wait to start anything.\\n>>>>>>\\n>>>>>> On Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:34:33 -0400, \\\"Lindgren, Caleb\\\"\\n>>>>>> <clindgren@g.harvard.edu<mailto:clindgren@g.harvard.edu>> said:\\n>>>>>>> Thanks for the heads up. I can't connect either. I logged in to the independent control console, and it says the chassis was opened this morning around 8 am, and then it was powered off. I'm on my way to lab right now, I'll inspect in person and update you.\\n>>>>>>>\\n>>>>>>> On Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:39:07 -0400, \\\"Bott, Alex Joseph\\\" <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu<mailto:alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu>> said:\\n>>>>>>>> Hi Caleb,\\n>>>>>>>>\\n>>>>>>>> I can't connect to the ardia this morning. It was fine last night around 10? VPN is working but the connection fails. I'm WFH today but wanted to give you a heads up.\\n>>>>>>>>\\n>>>>>>>> Thanks,\\n>>>>>>>> Alex\\n>>>>>>>>\\n>>>>>>\\n>>>>>\\n>>>\\n>>\\n>\\r\\n--5cce1de54cc5868dab01203aeb6a29fbb11f54543a3597a340f8e8526e78--\\r\\n\"" pid=11564
time="2026-11-03T12:37:21.381-05:00" level=info msg="RPC> gmail.Users.Messages.Send(email=\"me\" threadID=\"1a17d5f20bf72724\" msg=\"In-Reply-To: <MN2PR07MB59186154ED809FE0BC12F683C0692@MN2PR07MB5918.namprd07.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nMIME-Version: 1.0\\r\\nReferences: <MN2PR07MB59188388A51F44B3CD508E96C0602@MN2PR07MB5918.namprd07.prod.outlook.com> <CABAFTuv_ugieRfmjG6+rfRb377eFQDW5qNDfFzo1qrBzx8kYhQ@mail.gmail.com> <CABAFTuuLPh2snoVJB1rqU83kC5AjU=y00TGZHE348TaKJxAp_A@mail.gmail.com> <MN2PR07MB59188CE9E5189DDC994F36D4C0602@MN2PR07MB5918.namprd07.prod.outlook.com> <CABAFTutDnRO0Qc40PLPsY1PMHMv+GZUmz-PE2SQ7ZUM__vqNVA@mail.gmail.com> <MN2PR07MB5918C878B5DB77D5CD54F2F5C0602@MN2PR07MB5918.namprd07.prod.outlook.com> <CABAFTus0WwEpGwR3x8L4R66teQKZeGJ-3u6t_GgVLnpfHA8fvg@mail.gmail.com> <MN2PR07MB5918A9FFE0F70B6BC1B362B4C06F2@MN2PR07MB5918.namprd07.prod.outlook.com> <MN2PR07MB5918EE98E6FBB69F610FBF81C06A2@MN2PR07MB5918.namprd07.prod.outlook.com> <CABAFTutY3bHX1t+pJt3-L_CXeAsfp2H57bA=__dMWxW=ueBKVg@mail.gmail.com> <CABAFTuvv6d__0nCDGXmD7orwdTLn4AGV-_taAtFqmXP9p74Y-w@mail.gmail.com> <MN2PR07MB5918DF0D4332CA585C38AEBDC06A2@MN2PR07MB5918.namprd07.prod.outlook.com> <CABAFTusN6xoDN=oa78nm66JisT4V0C8gT1vZhUjiGbdwJT4L8w@mail.gmail.com> <MN2PR07MB59184B07AECCB5EE7F6F6B3DC0692@MN2PR07MB5918.namprd07.prod.outlook.com> <CABAFTuudQXu5vJwOyERFh-RNFWELvkTsh40uVDx_mHDmvHLVuA@mail.gmail.com> <MN2PR07MB59186154ED809FE0BC12F683C0692@MN2PR07MB5918.namprd07.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nSubject: Re: Ardia\\r\\nTo: \\\"Bott, Alex Joseph\\\" <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu>\\r\\nContent-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=\\\"5cce1de54cc5868dab01203aeb6a29fbb11f54543a3597a340f8e8526e78\\\"\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\n\\r\\n--5cce1de54cc5868dab01203aeb6a29fbb11f54543a3597a340f8e8526e78\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nOkay! It's all back up now.\\n\\nOn Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:17:18 -0500, \\\"Bott, Alex Joseph\\\" <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu> said:\\n> No worries. I probably won't start anything until tomorrow since I need to have Yuchen help me mount to standby.\\n> ________________________________\\n> From: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu>\\n> Sent: Tuesday, November 3, 2026 11:45 AM\\n> To: Bott, Alex Joseph <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu>\\n> Subject: Re: Ardia\\n>\\n> No problem! By the way, I do need to unplug the network switch briefly\\n> to rearrange some cables--I saw you're not currently logged in, but\\n> just FYI network access will be down for a minute while I do that.\\n>\\n> On Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:33:20 -0500, \\\"Bott, Alex Joseph\\\"\\n> <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu> said:\\n>> Awesome! Thanks again for managing the machine and dealing with this all!\\n>> ________________________________\\n>> From: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu>\\n>> Sent: Tuesday, November 3, 2026 11:31 AM\\n>> To: Bott, Alex Joseph <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu>\\n>> Subject: Re: Ardia\\n>>\\n>> It works now! New IP is 10.119.48.62\\n>>\\n>> On Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:23:50 -0500, \\\"Bott, Alex Joseph\\\"\\n>> <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu> said:\\n>>> Roger that, thanks again!\\n>>> ________________________________\\n>>> From: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu>\\n>>> Sent: Monday, November 2, 2026 4:34 PM\\n>>> To: Bott, Alex Joseph <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu>\\n>>> Subject: Re: Ardia\\n>>>\\n>>> Sounds like the issue is due to the switchbox that is between the\\n>>> computer and the wall socket. He said a guy will come by tomorrow\\n>>> morning to sort it out.\\n>>>\\n>>> On Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:59:10 -0500, \\\"Lindgren, Caleb\\\"\\n>>> <clindgren@g.harvard.edu> said:\\n>>>> Unfortunately nothing yet. I emailed Peter on Friday evening and told him it still wasn't working, and he said he'd have them look into it more on Monday, but that's the last I heard. I'll ping him again.\\n>>>>\\n>>>> On Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:55:59 -0500, \\\"Bott, Alex Joseph\\\" <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu> said:\\n>>>>> Hey Caleb,\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> Just wanted to see if there was any update. I'm eager to start looking at my last DIA data but understand if IT is slow rolling it.\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> Thanks,\\n>>>>> Alex\\n>>>>> ________________________________\\n>>>>> From: Bott, Alex Joseph <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu>\\n>>>>> Sent: Wednesday, October 28, 2026 2:39 PM\\n>>>>> To: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu>\\n>>>>> Subject: Re: Ardia\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> Ok sounds good, thanks for the update! I'll be in tomorrow and can help if needed.\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> Thanks for managing this! I think I'll back up my data on the Ardia to O2 tonight just in case.\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> Best,\\n>>>>> Alex\\n>>>>> ________________________________\\n>>>>> From: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu>\\n>>>>> Sent: Wednesday, October 28, 2026 2:35 PM\\n>>>>> To: Bott, Alex Joseph <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu>\\n>>>>> Subject: Re: Ardia\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> Just FYI, the guys getting us the new table that we're going to put the Ardia on in the new room said they actually can't bring the table until tomorrow, so we're going to have to wait until tomorrow to move it. I'll keep you posted.\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> Bott, Alex Joseph <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu<mailto:alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu>> 於 2026年10月27日週二 15:05 寫道：\\n>>>>> Ah man ok. Well I'll just log in and survey the damage. I think I had logging points along the run but let's see.\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> Thanks for taking care of everything. Very hopeful that the new home will further reduce issues.\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> Best,\\n>>>>> Alex\\n>>>>> ________________________________\\n>>>>> From: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu<mailto:clindgren@g.harvard.edu>>\\n>>>>> Sent: Tuesday, October 27, 2026 3:03 PM\\n>>>>> To: Bott, Alex Joseph <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu<mailto:alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu>>\\n>>>>> Subject: Re: Ardia\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> Yeah, it was spontaneous. JP said he hadn't touched it or noticed\\n>>>>> anything weird. The cover was displaced when I came in this morning,\\n>>>>> so maybe it just got bumped.\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> What I ended up doing was unplugging the power, taking off the cover,\\n>>>>> taking out the fan cage and airflow distributor, and then reseating\\n>>>>> some cables that the logs flagged as having issues. Unsure exactly\\n>>>>> which step fixed it, but the diagnostics all look good now. I checked\\n>>>>> on Docker and everything was gone, so I went ahead and did the Sysbox\\n>>>>> install.\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> Good to go now, but I wouldn't start anything today that will still be\\n>>>>> running tomorrow--JP said he's got someone coming in tomorrow to\\n>>>>> install a table in the supply room closet between Shelly and David's\\n>>>>> benches, so we'll power the machine off and move it there tomorrow.\\n>>>>> Hopefully putting it in a more isolated environment will fix these\\n>>>>> issues we've been having.\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> Thanks for your help with this!\\n>>>>>\\n>>>>> On Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:23:13 -0400, \\\"Bott, Alex Joseph\\\"\\n>>>>> <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu<mailto:alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu>> said:\\n>>>>>> Sounds good, I assume it went down spontaneously? If the machine fully went down I bet my long running jobs died, so maybe that would indicate a good time for your docker fix.\\n>>>>>> ________________________________\\n>>>>>> From: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu<mailto:clindgren@g.harvard.edu>>\\n>>>>>> Sent: Tuesday, October 27, 2026 1:14 PM\\n>>>>>> To: Bott, Alex Joseph <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu<mailto:alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu>>\\n>>>>>> Subject: Re: Ardia\\n>>>>>>\\n>>>>>> It boots now, but I'm still debugging so wait to start anything.\\n>>>>>>\\n>>>>>> On Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:34:33 -0400, \\\"Lindgren, Caleb\\\"\\n>>>>>> <clindgren@g.harvard.edu<mailto:clindgren@g.harvard.edu>> said:\\n>>>>>>> Thanks for the heads up. I can't connect either. I logged in to the independent control console, and it says the chassis was opened this morning around 8 am, and then it was powered off. I'm on my way to lab right now, I'll inspect in person and update you.\\n>>>>>>>\\n>>>>>>> On Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:39:07 -0400, \\\"Bott, Alex Joseph\\\" <alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu<mailto:alex_bott@hms.harvard.edu>> said:\\n>>>>>>>> Hi Caleb,\\n>>>>>>>>\\n>>>>>>>> I can't connect to the ardia this morning. It was fine last night around 10? VPN is working but the connection fails. I'm WFH today but wanted to give you a heads up.\\n>>>>>>>>\\n>>>>>>>> Thanks,\\n>>>>>>>> Alex\\n>>>>>>>>\\n>>>>>>\\n>>>>>\\n>>>\\n>>\\n>\\r\\n--5cce1de54cc5868dab01203aeb6a29fbb11f54543a3597a340f8e8526e78--\\r\\n\") => <nil> 452.891216ms" pid=11564
