time="2026-11-04T15:54:55.323-05:00" level=info msg="Final message: \"In-Reply-To: <CA+gHYQueutoiQTzn4DXM6TQgm1b93uLcXWAXSzBxjSsz69vcTA@mail.gmail.com>\\r\\nMIME-Version: 1.0\\r\\nReferences: <CA+gHYQsnoYJK8D0mUW4CSK_eHEV=5_avpygQaF6aRno7RXkeUQ@mail.gmail.com> <CABAFTuukCMeuS1-5oNoyRuNiYJ=qQ0xf1Pp+E6udsGXtk0JYZw@mail.gmail.com> <CA+gHYQueutoiQTzn4DXM6TQgm1b93uLcXWAXSzBxjSsz69vcTA@mail.gmail.com>\\r\\nSubject: Re: SSQB AAP - Hello!\\r\\nTo: \\\"Zac Fedder\\\" <zac.fedder@gmail.com>\\r\\nContent-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=\\\"068ad0a9676bb27e27e2b044dbe80d96dd964d921e289698afd0388aa955\\\"\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\n\\r\\n--068ad0a9676bb27e27e2b044dbe80d96dd964d921e289698afd0388aa955\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nSounds good, talk to you then!\\n\\nOn Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:25:09 -0500, Zac Fedder <zac.fedder@gmail.com> said:\\n> Hey Caleb,\\n>\\n> Let’s do tonight at 8pm my time. Looking forward to chatting! I can send a\\n> Zoom link closer to the time.\\n>\\n> Cheers,\\n> Zac\\n>\\n>\\n> Zachary Fedder\\n>\\n> Associate Research Scientist, Protein Engineering\\n>\\n> AbCellera Biologics\\n>\\n> Vancouver, BC\\n>\\n> Work email: zachary.fedder@abcellera.com\\n>\\n> LinkedIn\\n> <https://www.linkedin.com/in/zachary-fedder?utm_source=share_via&utm_content=profile&utm_medium=member_ios>\\n>\\n> On Wed, Nov 4, 2026 at 12:46 Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu>\\n> wrote:\\n>\\n>> Hi Zac,\\n>>\\n>> Good to hear from you! Yeah I'm happy to give feedback on your\\n>> statement of purpose and personal statement, send them over whenever\\n>> you're ready. As far as meeting, I could do anytime between 5 pm and 9\\n>> pm tonight your time, or between 6 am and 9 am tomorrow. If neither of\\n>> those work we can figure something else out, sorry for not responding\\n>> faster.\\n>>\\n>> Best,\\n>>\\n>> Caleb\\n>>\\n>> On Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:22:59 -0500, Zac Fedder <zac.fedder@gmail.com> said:\\n>> > Hi Caleb,\\n>> >\\n>> > Great to meet you virtually and thank you so much for volunteering to\\n>> > support me through this application process, I really appreciate it.\\n>> >\\n>> > Here is a bit of background on me (and I would be happy to send you an\\n>> > updated CV as well):\\n>> > I graduated from Western University in Ontario, Canada, in 2022 with an\\n>> > Honours Specialization in Genetics and Biochemistry. I started working\\n>> as a\\n>> > Research Technician at AbCellera Biologics in Vancouver, Canada, in 2023\\n>> > and have since been promoted to Associate Research Scientist. I am on the\\n>> > Protein Engineering team, where I specialise in therapeutic antibody\\n>> > discovery and engineering with mutational, synthetic, and repertoire\\n>> > libraries screened using phage display. My experience is heavily skewed\\n>> > toward the wet lab, although I have learned a lot on the computational\\n>> side\\n>> > over the past few years.\\n>> >\\n>> > At this point in my career, I am looking to go back to school to\\n>> complete a\\n>> > PhD in a program that will significantly help me progress professionally\\n>> > (not just going back to school for the sake of doing a PhD and getting\\n>> > research experience, which I already have in my current job). I am really\\n>> > looking to expand my expertise in the computational side to complement my\\n>> > continued learning in the wet lab - a combination that is perfectly\\n>> > exemplified in a program like SSQB. Generally, I am looking to become a\\n>> > more well-rounded scientist, which is something that is difficult to\\n>> pursue\\n>> > when filling a very specific niche at a biotech company.\\n>> >\\n>> > Another big incentive for applying to this program is the deep industry\\n>> > ties and the fantastic innovation ecosystem surrounding Harvard, both on\\n>> > and off campus. Ultimately, I want the opportunity to found or co-found\\n>> > start-ups, and doing this out of an academic lab at an institution like\\n>> > Harvard is by far the best route.\\n>> >\\n>> > I go into more detail on my PhD project interests and my incentives for\\n>> > applying to Harvard SSQB in my Statement of Purpose and my Personal\\n>> > Statement. I would be happy to provide these as well once I have a\\n>> cleaner\\n>> > draft of them by the end of the week. Any feedback and comments on those\\n>> > would be hugely appreciated!\\n>> >\\n>> > I also have a few other questions about my application that I would love\\n>> to\\n>> > discuss with you.\\n>> >\\n>> > I am available to meet once per week, as recommended by the AAP mentee\\n>> > guide that Maile shared. However, I understand you are quite busy as a\\n>> PhD\\n>> > student, so please let me know if this would work for you or not.\\n>> >\\n>> > Given I am working full time right now, meeting before 9am or after 5pm\\n>> > would be ideal, although my schedule is relatively flexible whenever I\\n>> can\\n>> > move experiments around. Weekends also work well for me. I am in\\n>> Vancouver,\\n>> > BC, so on Pacific Time (PCT, UCT-7).\\n>> >\\n>> > Thank you again for volunteering for AAP. I look forward to chatting!\\n>> >\\n>> > Best regards,\\n>> > Zac\\n>> >\\n>> > --\\n>> >\\n>> > Zachary Fedder\\n>> >\\n>> > Associate Research Scientist, Protein Engineering\\n>> >\\n>> > AbCellera Biologics\\n>> >\\n>> > Vancouver, BC\\n>> >\\n>> > Work email: zachary.fedder@abcellera.com\\n>> >\\n>> > LinkedIn\\n>> > <\\n>> https://www.linkedin.com/in/zachary-fedder?utm_source=share_via&utm_content=profile&utm_medium=member_ios\\n>> >\\n>> >\\n>>\\n>\\r\\n--068ad0a9676bb27e27e2b044dbe80d96dd964d921e289698afd0388aa955--\\r\\n\"" pid=20708
time="2026-11-04T15:54:55.728-05:00" level=info msg="RPC> gmail.Users.Messages.Send(email=\"me\" threadID=\"1a19e5bff424c924\" msg=\"In-Reply-To: <CA+gHYQueutoiQTzn4DXM6TQgm1b93uLcXWAXSzBxjSsz69vcTA@mail.gmail.com>\\r\\nMIME-Version: 1.0\\r\\nReferences: <CA+gHYQsnoYJK8D0mUW4CSK_eHEV=5_avpygQaF6aRno7RXkeUQ@mail.gmail.com> <CABAFTuukCMeuS1-5oNoyRuNiYJ=qQ0xf1Pp+E6udsGXtk0JYZw@mail.gmail.com> <CA+gHYQueutoiQTzn4DXM6TQgm1b93uLcXWAXSzBxjSsz69vcTA@mail.gmail.com>\\r\\nSubject: Re: SSQB AAP - Hello!\\r\\nTo: \\\"Zac Fedder\\\" <zac.fedder@gmail.com>\\r\\nContent-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=\\\"068ad0a9676bb27e27e2b044dbe80d96dd964d921e289698afd0388aa955\\\"\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\n\\r\\n--068ad0a9676bb27e27e2b044dbe80d96dd964d921e289698afd0388aa955\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nSounds good, talk to you then!\\n\\nOn Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:25:09 -0500, Zac Fedder <zac.fedder@gmail.com> said:\\n> Hey Caleb,\\n>\\n> Let’s do tonight at 8pm my time. Looking forward to chatting! I can send a\\n> Zoom link closer to the time.\\n>\\n> Cheers,\\n> Zac\\n>\\n>\\n> Zachary Fedder\\n>\\n> Associate Research Scientist, Protein Engineering\\n>\\n> AbCellera Biologics\\n>\\n> Vancouver, BC\\n>\\n> Work email: zachary.fedder@abcellera.com\\n>\\n> LinkedIn\\n> <https://www.linkedin.com/in/zachary-fedder?utm_source=share_via&utm_content=profile&utm_medium=member_ios>\\n>\\n> On Wed, Nov 4, 2026 at 12:46 Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu>\\n> wrote:\\n>\\n>> Hi Zac,\\n>>\\n>> Good to hear from you! Yeah I'm happy to give feedback on your\\n>> statement of purpose and personal statement, send them over whenever\\n>> you're ready. As far as meeting, I could do anytime between 5 pm and 9\\n>> pm tonight your time, or between 6 am and 9 am tomorrow. If neither of\\n>> those work we can figure something else out, sorry for not responding\\n>> faster.\\n>>\\n>> Best,\\n>>\\n>> Caleb\\n>>\\n>> On Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:22:59 -0500, Zac Fedder <zac.fedder@gmail.com> said:\\n>> > Hi Caleb,\\n>> >\\n>> > Great to meet you virtually and thank you so much for volunteering to\\n>> > support me through this application process, I really appreciate it.\\n>> >\\n>> > Here is a bit of background on me (and I would be happy to send you an\\n>> > updated CV as well):\\n>> > I graduated from Western University in Ontario, Canada, in 2022 with an\\n>> > Honours Specialization in Genetics and Biochemistry. I started working\\n>> as a\\n>> > Research Technician at AbCellera Biologics in Vancouver, Canada, in 2023\\n>> > and have since been promoted to Associate Research Scientist. I am on the\\n>> > Protein Engineering team, where I specialise in therapeutic antibody\\n>> > discovery and engineering with mutational, synthetic, and repertoire\\n>> > libraries screened using phage display. My experience is heavily skewed\\n>> > toward the wet lab, although I have learned a lot on the computational\\n>> side\\n>> > over the past few years.\\n>> >\\n>> > At this point in my career, I am looking to go back to school to\\n>> complete a\\n>> > PhD in a program that will significantly help me progress professionally\\n>> > (not just going back to school for the sake of doing a PhD and getting\\n>> > research experience, which I already have in my current job). I am really\\n>> > looking to expand my expertise in the computational side to complement my\\n>> > continued learning in the wet lab - a combination that is perfectly\\n>> > exemplified in a program like SSQB. Generally, I am looking to become a\\n>> > more well-rounded scientist, which is something that is difficult to\\n>> pursue\\n>> > when filling a very specific niche at a biotech company.\\n>> >\\n>> > Another big incentive for applying to this program is the deep industry\\n>> > ties and the fantastic innovation ecosystem surrounding Harvard, both on\\n>> > and off campus. Ultimately, I want the opportunity to found or co-found\\n>> > start-ups, and doing this out of an academic lab at an institution like\\n>> > Harvard is by far the best route.\\n>> >\\n>> > I go into more detail on my PhD project interests and my incentives for\\n>> > applying to Harvard SSQB in my Statement of Purpose and my Personal\\n>> > Statement. I would be happy to provide these as well once I have a\\n>> cleaner\\n>> > draft of them by the end of the week. Any feedback and comments on those\\n>> > would be hugely appreciated!\\n>> >\\n>> > I also have a few other questions about my application that I would love\\n>> to\\n>> > discuss with you.\\n>> >\\n>> > I am available to meet once per week, as recommended by the AAP mentee\\n>> > guide that Maile shared. However, I understand you are quite busy as a\\n>> PhD\\n>> > student, so please let me know if this would work for you or not.\\n>> >\\n>> > Given I am working full time right now, meeting before 9am or after 5pm\\n>> > would be ideal, although my schedule is relatively flexible whenever I\\n>> can\\n>> > move experiments around. Weekends also work well for me. I am in\\n>> Vancouver,\\n>> > BC, so on Pacific Time (PCT, UCT-7).\\n>> >\\n>> > Thank you again for volunteering for AAP. I look forward to chatting!\\n>> >\\n>> > Best regards,\\n>> > Zac\\n>> >\\n>> > --\\n>> >\\n>> > Zachary Fedder\\n>> >\\n>> > Associate Research Scientist, Protein Engineering\\n>> >\\n>> > AbCellera Biologics\\n>> >\\n>> > Vancouver, BC\\n>> >\\n>> > Work email: zachary.fedder@abcellera.com\\n>> >\\n>> > LinkedIn\\n>> > <\\n>> https://www.linkedin.com/in/zachary-fedder?utm_source=share_via&utm_content=profile&utm_medium=member_ios\\n>> >\\n>> >\\n>>\\n>\\r\\n--068ad0a9676bb27e27e2b044dbe80d96dd964d921e289698afd0388aa955--\\r\\n\") => <nil> 404.025992ms" pid=20708
