time="2026-11-04T17:02:50.483-05:00" level=info msg="Final message: \"In-Reply-To: <BL4PR07MB103342C4A11F1AD28F80CEF1C82682@BL4PR07MB10334.namprd07.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nMIME-Version: 1.0\\r\\nReferences: <BL4PR07MB103342C4A11F1AD28F80CEF1C82682@BL4PR07MB10334.namprd07.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nSubject: Re: OT-2 robot\\r\\nTo: \\\"Pontano Vaites, Laura\\\" <lpvaites@hms.harvard.edu>\\r\\nContent-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=\\\"6c1ab4902578e8ce7b9028f1932fc4f9b4a1f250ae28d3806f8622b1d51b\\\"\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\n\\r\\n--6c1ab4902578e8ce7b9028f1932fc4f9b4a1f250ae28d3806f8622b1d51b\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nHi Laura,\\n\\nYeah happy to talk! Tomorrow is best for me, I'll be gone Friday at a retreat for my program. I'm free anytime before 5:30, let me know when is good for you.\\n\\nCaleb.\\n\\nOn Wed, 4 Nov 2026 16:16:10 -0500, \\\"Pontano Vaites, Laura\\\" <lpvaites@hms.harvard.edu> said:\\n> Hi Caleb,\\n>\\n> JP mentioned that you have been using the OT-2 robot quite a bit. I was wondering if you might have a few minutes tomorrow or Friday to show me some of the features. I'm trying to see if we can leverage it in a robust way to handle our CRBN pulldown assays and possibly transfer the 400uL pulldown volume in batches to a PCR plate for washing on the ring magnet. Please let me know your thoughts.\\n>\\n> Thanks,\\n>\\n> Laura\\n>\\r\\n--6c1ab4902578e8ce7b9028f1932fc4f9b4a1f250ae28d3806f8622b1d51b--\\r\\n\"" pid=27254
time="2026-11-04T17:02:50.934-05:00" level=info msg="RPC> gmail.Users.Messages.Send(email=\"me\" threadID=\"1a1a86b614369f31\" msg=\"In-Reply-To: <BL4PR07MB103342C4A11F1AD28F80CEF1C82682@BL4PR07MB10334.namprd07.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nMIME-Version: 1.0\\r\\nReferences: <BL4PR07MB103342C4A11F1AD28F80CEF1C82682@BL4PR07MB10334.namprd07.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nSubject: Re: OT-2 robot\\r\\nTo: \\\"Pontano Vaites, Laura\\\" <lpvaites@hms.harvard.edu>\\r\\nContent-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=\\\"6c1ab4902578e8ce7b9028f1932fc4f9b4a1f250ae28d3806f8622b1d51b\\\"\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\n\\r\\n--6c1ab4902578e8ce7b9028f1932fc4f9b4a1f250ae28d3806f8622b1d51b\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nHi Laura,\\n\\nYeah happy to talk! Tomorrow is best for me, I'll be gone Friday at a retreat for my program. I'm free anytime before 5:30, let me know when is good for you.\\n\\nCaleb.\\n\\nOn Wed, 4 Nov 2026 16:16:10 -0500, \\\"Pontano Vaites, Laura\\\" <lpvaites@hms.harvard.edu> said:\\n> Hi Caleb,\\n>\\n> JP mentioned that you have been using the OT-2 robot quite a bit. I was wondering if you might have a few minutes tomorrow or Friday to show me some of the features. I'm trying to see if we can leverage it in a robust way to handle our CRBN pulldown assays and possibly transfer the 400uL pulldown volume in batches to a PCR plate for washing on the ring magnet. Please let me know your thoughts.\\n>\\n> Thanks,\\n>\\n> Laura\\n>\\r\\n--6c1ab4902578e8ce7b9028f1932fc4f9b4a1f250ae28d3806f8622b1d51b--\\r\\n\") => <nil> 450.897829ms" pid=27254
