time="2026-11-05T11:27:10.167-05:00" level=info msg="Final message: \"In-Reply-To: <BL4PR07MB103340A9DEE6C253226CDDD8782772@BL4PR07MB10334.namprd07.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nMIME-Version: 1.0\\r\\nReferences: <BL4PR07MB103342C4A11F1AD28F80CEF1C82682@BL4PR07MB10334.namprd07.prod.outlook.com> <CABAFTutjOVKwXMqq6O_BPZbi6C-Zto9Z33t+hqiPv9GYH=uYsQ@mail.gmail.com> <BL4PR07MB103340A9DEE6C253226CDDD8782772@BL4PR07MB10334.namprd07.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nSubject: Re: OT-2 robot\\r\\nTo: \\\"Pontano Vaites, Laura\\\" <lpvaites@hms.harvard.edu>\\r\\nContent-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=\\\"3aa10f8d7d1fc6b02d2c6cdc13c083707f3e205cada0ed3b1c57e1639fa7\\\"\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\n\\r\\n--3aa10f8d7d1fc6b02d2c6cdc13c083707f3e205cada0ed3b1c57e1639fa7\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\n2 pm is great! Sounds good.\\n\\nOn Thu, 5 Nov 2026 11:20:08 -0500, \\\"Pontano Vaites, Laura\\\" <lpvaites@hms.harvard.edu> said:\\n> Hi Caleb,\\n>\\n> Would this afternoon work for you, maybe around 2pm? I'm not going to try an experiment yet but just have a bunch of questions about what it can handle and best plates/materials to purchase for the experiment.\\n>\\n> Thanks,\\n>\\n> Laura\\n> ________________________________\\n> From: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu>\\n> Sent: Wednesday, November 4, 2026 5:02 PM\\n> To: Pontano Vaites, Laura <lpvaites@hms.harvard.edu>\\n> Subject: Re: OT-2 robot\\n>\\n> Hi Laura,\\n>\\n> Yeah happy to talk! Tomorrow is best for me, I'll be gone Friday at a\\n> retreat for my program. I'm free anytime before 5:30, let me know when\\n> is good for you.\\n>\\n> Caleb.\\n>\\n> On Wed, 4 Nov 2026 16:16:10 -0500, \\\"Pontano Vaites, Laura\\\"\\n> <lpvaites@hms.harvard.edu> said:\\n>> Hi Caleb,\\n>>\\n>> JP mentioned that you have been using the OT-2 robot quite a bit. I was wondering if you might have a few minutes tomorrow or Friday to show me some of the features. I'm trying to see if we can leverage it in a robust way to handle our CRBN pulldown assays and possibly transfer the 400uL pulldown volume in batches to a PCR plate for washing on the ring magnet. Please let me know your thoughts.\\n>>\\n>> Thanks,\\n>>\\n>> Laura\\n>>\\n>\\r\\n--3aa10f8d7d1fc6b02d2c6cdc13c083707f3e205cada0ed3b1c57e1639fa7--\\r\\n\"" pid=26544
time="2026-11-05T11:27:10.585-05:00" level=info msg="RPC> gmail.Users.Messages.Send(email=\"me\" threadID=\"1a1a86b614369f31\" msg=\"In-Reply-To: <BL4PR07MB103340A9DEE6C253226CDDD8782772@BL4PR07MB10334.namprd07.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nMIME-Version: 1.0\\r\\nReferences: <BL4PR07MB103342C4A11F1AD28F80CEF1C82682@BL4PR07MB10334.namprd07.prod.outlook.com> <CABAFTutjOVKwXMqq6O_BPZbi6C-Zto9Z33t+hqiPv9GYH=uYsQ@mail.gmail.com> <BL4PR07MB103340A9DEE6C253226CDDD8782772@BL4PR07MB10334.namprd07.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nSubject: Re: OT-2 robot\\r\\nTo: \\\"Pontano Vaites, Laura\\\" <lpvaites@hms.harvard.edu>\\r\\nContent-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=\\\"3aa10f8d7d1fc6b02d2c6cdc13c083707f3e205cada0ed3b1c57e1639fa7\\\"\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\n\\r\\n--3aa10f8d7d1fc6b02d2c6cdc13c083707f3e205cada0ed3b1c57e1639fa7\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\n2 pm is great! Sounds good.\\n\\nOn Thu, 5 Nov 2026 11:20:08 -0500, \\\"Pontano Vaites, Laura\\\" <lpvaites@hms.harvard.edu> said:\\n> Hi Caleb,\\n>\\n> Would this afternoon work for you, maybe around 2pm? I'm not going to try an experiment yet but just have a bunch of questions about what it can handle and best plates/materials to purchase for the experiment.\\n>\\n> Thanks,\\n>\\n> Laura\\n> ________________________________\\n> From: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu>\\n> Sent: Wednesday, November 4, 2026 5:02 PM\\n> To: Pontano Vaites, Laura <lpvaites@hms.harvard.edu>\\n> Subject: Re: OT-2 robot\\n>\\n> Hi Laura,\\n>\\n> Yeah happy to talk! Tomorrow is best for me, I'll be gone Friday at a\\n> retreat for my program. I'm free anytime before 5:30, let me know when\\n> is good for you.\\n>\\n> Caleb.\\n>\\n> On Wed, 4 Nov 2026 16:16:10 -0500, \\\"Pontano Vaites, Laura\\\"\\n> <lpvaites@hms.harvard.edu> said:\\n>> Hi Caleb,\\n>>\\n>> JP mentioned that you have been using the OT-2 robot quite a bit. I was wondering if you might have a few minutes tomorrow or Friday to show me some of the features. I'm trying to see if we can leverage it in a robust way to handle our CRBN pulldown assays and possibly transfer the 400uL pulldown volume in batches to a PCR plate for washing on the ring magnet. Please let me know your thoughts.\\n>>\\n>> Thanks,\\n>>\\n>> Laura\\n>>\\n>\\r\\n--3aa10f8d7d1fc6b02d2c6cdc13c083707f3e205cada0ed3b1c57e1639fa7--\\r\\n\") => <nil> 418.110809ms" pid=26544
