time="2026-11-05T11:33:18.668-05:00" level=info msg="Final message: \"In-Reply-To: <MW4PR19MB6625CA0680B3217C70D47914C6772@MW4PR19MB6625.namprd19.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nMIME-Version: 1.0\\r\\nReferences: <CAP_LnvHUVY4KmUOFj21d-Wm8juzKUb_xb2yA40Nzk2gKRpQJfQ@mail.gmail.com> <MW4PR19MB66250E8CE109034F266AB70FC6692@MW4PR19MB6625.namprd19.prod.outlook.com> <CABAFTuvGw2dug7wYkb6XfK8-hTO_6KLpOYowHjtCzPjRv1=s3g@mail.gmail.com> <MW4PR19MB6625CA0680B3217C70D47914C6772@MW4PR19MB6625.namprd19.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nSubject: Re: [EXT] Harvard SSQB application assistance program mentor-mentee matching\\r\\nTo: \\\"Mount, Kaia Helen - (kmount)\\\" <kmount@arizona.edu>\\r\\nContent-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=\\\"5b221d15c03ee33ce3a179087dfbd09119f9106f396335361fba03c07db0\\\"\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\n\\r\\n--5b221d15c03ee33ce3a179087dfbd09119f9106f396335361fba03c07db0\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nHi Kaia,\\n\\nNo worries! Let's meet at 2 pm MST. Here's a Zoom link: \\n\\nCaleb Lindgren is inviting you to a scheduled Zoom meeting.\\nTime: Nov 5, 2026 02:00 PM Arizona\\nhttps://harvard.zoom.us/j/96141879880?pwd=SbD21RayM27jNhA7qDjwQRuEnEKrBR.1\\nPassword: 809843\\n\\nTalk to you then,\\n\\nCaleb\\n\\nOn Thu, 5 Nov 2026 10:58:05 -0500, \\\"Mount, Kaia Helen - (kmount)\\\" <kmount@arizona.edu> said:\\n> Dear Caleb,\\n>\\n> Thank you for getting back to me, and I apologize for the late response. I am available today from 11:00 am to 3:00 pm MST. If that is too short notice, please let me know what time works best for you and I will happily adjust.\\n>\\n> I would also really appreciate your feedback on my essays, and I will send them over shortly.\\n>\\n> Best,\\n> Kaia\\n>\\n> ________________________________\\n> From: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu>\\n> Sent: Wednesday, November 4, 2026 12:59 PM\\n> To: Mount, Kaia Helen - (kmount) <kmount@arizona.edu>\\n> Subject: Re: [EXT] Harvard SSQB application assistance program mentor-mentee matching\\n>\\n> External Email\\n>\\n> Hi Kaia,\\n>\\n> Great to hear from you! I'm happy to meet, could you do sometime\\n> between 9 am and 3 pm your time tomorrow? Also happy to give feedback\\n> on your essays, send them over whenever you're ready.\\n>\\n> Best,\\n>\\n> Caleb\\n>\\n> On Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:38:35 -0500, \\\"Mount, Kaia Helen - (kmount)\\\"\\n> <kmount@arizona.edu> said:\\n>> Dear Caleb,\\n>>\\n>> It is great to meet you! My name is Kaia Mount and I am a senior at the University of Arizona majoring in Molecular & Cellular Biology and Biochemistry. I currently do cell signaling and systems biology research studying how the Target of Rapamycin Complex 1 (TORC1) signaling pathway regulates translation and amino acid transport. I am applying to PhD programs this cycle and am interested in using quantitative and systems approaches, such as proteomics and interaction networks, to understand how signaling and translation connect genotype to phenotype in cells. I am very excited to be matched with you through the SSQBio Application Assistance Program.\\n>>\\n>> There are two main things I hope to get out of this program. First, I would love to meet with you once to hear about your approach to the SSQB application and what you like most about the program. Second, if you are willing, I would greatly appreciate any feedback you could give on my application essays.\\n>>\\n>> In terms of frequency, I am happy to follow whatever works best for your schedule. One meeting to start, plus email exchanges as needed when I have drafts ready, would be wonderful. I am located in Arizona (MST) and can be flexible with timing.\\n>>\\n>> Thank you so much for taking the time to mentor me. I look forward to hearing from you!\\n>>\\n>> Very best,\\n>> Kaia\\n>>\\n>> Kaia Mount\\n>>\\n>> Molecular and Cellular Biology I Class of 2027\\n>>\\n>> Capaldi Lab\\n>>\\n>> W.A. Franke Honors College\\n>> The University of Arizona\\n>>\\n>> ________________________________\\n>> From: Hirschmann, Maile <mailejim@g.harvard.edu>\\n>> Sent: Monday, November 2, 2026 12:59 PM\\n>> To: Caleb Lindgren <clindgren@g.harvard.edu>; Mount, Kaia Helen - (kmount) <kmount@arizona.edu>\\n>> Cc: Carlos Morales <carlosmorales@g.harvard.edu>\\n>> Subject: [EXT] Harvard SSQB application assistance program mentor-mentee matching\\n>>\\n>>\\n>> External Email\\n>>\\n>> ________________________________\\n>> Dear Kaia and Caleb,\\n>>\\n>> We have matched you as part of the SSQBio Application Assistance Program (AAP) for this application cycle! Attached here are the mentee guidelines. Mentors should have received their guidelines in a separate email. We recommend that mentees email their mentors separately from this email to begin your email exchanges. In this email, introduce yourself, describe what you would like to get out of the program, and establish what frequency you’d like to communicate with your mentor.\\n>>\\n>> Let us know if either of you have any questions now or later in the AAP mentoring process.\\n>>\\n>> Happy matching!\\n>> Maile and Carlos\\n>>\\n>> Mentee guidelines: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JLGIXbHLtGximivA8CN5HHYBChRnO5ABZWMaCWIdEJw/edit?tab=t.0<https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JLGIXbHLtGximivA8CN5HHYBChRnO5ABZWMaCWIdEJw/edit?tab=t.0><https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JLGIXbHLtGximivA8CN5HHYBChRnO5ABZWMaCWIdEJw/edit?tab=t.0<https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JLGIXbHLtGximivA8CN5HHYBChRnO5ABZWMaCWIdEJw/edit?tab=t.0>>\\n>>\\n>\\r\\n--5b221d15c03ee33ce3a179087dfbd09119f9106f396335361fba03c07db0--\\r\\n\"" pid=28189
